{"id":"h157","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"science-physics","question":"One of the tubes of a Rayleighrefractometeris filled with air, the other is evacuated. Then the second tube is filled with air at the same temperature and pressure as the first tube. During this process 98 fringes are seen to pass the field of view. What is the index of refraction of the air if sodium light is used and the tubes are each 20 cm long?\nIs the correct answer \"1.00069\"?","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":"TIGER-Lab/MMLU-Pro, test split","claims":[{"text":"The correct index of refraction is about 1.00029, not 1.00069.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Filling one tube changes the optical path by (n-1)L, and each fringe corresponds to a path change of one wavelength.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.5,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The fringe count is given by N = (n-1)L/λ.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.5,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"An index of 1.00069 would require n-1 ≈ 6.9e-4, implying a wavelength of about 1.4 μm, far from sodium light.","confidence":0.85,"lean":-1,"theta":1.3352,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Doubling the path (double pass) would give n-1 ≈ 1.4e-4, which does not match 1.00069 either.","confidence":0.8,"lean":-0.7,"theta":1.2566,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The standard single-pass relation with sodium wavelength about 589 nm gives a consistent value.","confidence":0.85,"lean":-0.8,"theta":1.3352,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Calculation: n-1 = 98 × 589e-9 / 0.20 ≈ 2.89e-4, so n ≈ 1.00029.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Nothing in the setup obviously supports 1.00069.","confidence":0.8,"lean":-0.8,"theta":1.2566,"phi":-3.1416}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0